# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages / compatible CDN — HTTP redirect rules
# Reference: https://specification.website/spec/seo/
# Reference: https://specification.website/spec/seo/redirects/

# Ensure canonical URL: strip trailing slash on non-root paths (optional)
# HTTP -> HTTPS. The `!` forces this ahead of the SPA rewrite below, so plain
# HTTP is never served. This is a host-level redirect, so it has to be the
# first rule. GitHub Pages ignores this whole file (it is Cloudflare/Netlify
# syntax) — there the equivalent is the "Enforce HTTPS" setting in the repo's
# Pages configuration, which is not expressible as a file. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
http://lotus.nprod.net/*  https://lotus.nprod.net/:splat  301!

# SPA fallback: redirect unknown routes to index.html (200 = rewrite, not 301).
# Excludes static asset paths so the Ketcher iframe and WASM bundle load directly.
!/assets/*
!/wasm/*
!/favicon*
!/apple-touch-icon*
!/android-chrome*
!/site.webmanifest
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml
!/llms.txt
!/humans.txt
!/.well-known/*
/*  /index.html  200
